1
00:02:05,679 --> 00:02:10,560
<v Woman>Morning, thanks for calling Metro Link. Is there anything I can do for you? 


2
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:16,238
<v Man>Good morning, I would like to go to Harbour City tomorrow before 11 a.m., eh, from Bayswater. 


3
00:02:16,238 --> 00:02:18,708
<v Woman>Well, for Bayswater...  


4
00:02:18,708 --> 00:02:24,962
<v Man> Oh..., no, no. From Bayswater, where I am currently living, but Harbour City is my destination.


5
00:02:24,962 --> 00:02:33,034
<v Woman>Sorry. That means, Bayswater to Harbour City. Which mode of vehicles do you prefer, by bus or train? 


6
00:02:33,034 --> 00:02:37,703
<v Man>In fact, I have no preference, only if it brought me to Harbour faster. 


7
00:02:37,703 --> 00:02:48,829
<v Woman>Well, if you take an express train, you'll be right in Harbour within an hour from departure. Let's see, yes, I recommend you to get on the 9:30 a.m. express. 


8
00:02:48,829 --> 00:02:53,226
<v Man>Sounds perfect. So, at which station should I get on the train? 


9
00:02:53,226 --> 00:02:55,912
<v Woman>Helendale is the nearest station to you. 

10
00:02:55,912 --> 00:02:58,182
<v Man>Henlensvale? Did you say that? 


11
00:02:58,182 --> 00:03:06,908
<v Woman>No, Helendale, that's H-E-L-E-N-D-A-L-E

12
00:03:06,908 --> 00:03:09,154
<v Man>Then how can I get there fastest? 


13
00:03:09,154 --> 00:03:28,387
<v Woman>Umm... Let me see, please wait a minute, I need to have a look. It says you probably have two options for the routes: the first one is the 706 bus from Bayswater Shopping Centre to Central Street; there will be another bus that can take you to the train station. 

14
00:03:28,387 --> 00:03:37,812
<v Woman>Or if you don't mind walking directly to the Central Street, like couple of kilometres, then you can take the bus there bringing you to the train station. 


15
00:03:37,802 --> 00:03:41,383
<v Man>Sure, but which bus is that, the one in Central Street? 

16
00:03:41,383 --> 00:03:47,607
<v Woman>The 702 will take... oh, sorry, it's the 782 that will take you to the station 


17
00:03:47,607 --> 00:03:54,985
<v Man>I believe walking will be fine, so option two might seem better to me. When should I arrive at Central street to catch the bus?


18
00:03:54,985 --> 00:04:14,908
<v Woman>There are two buses that you can catch up and get the station on time, one just before 9 o'clock, one right after. Yet in the morning, it might be better to take the earlier one just in case of a traffic jam or something like that. I'd like to say the 8:55 one is more reassuring than the 9:05 one. 


19
00:04:14,908 --> 00:04:18,914
<v Man>Sure, I don't want to miss the train, so the five to nine one will be better.


20
00:05:01,937 --> 00:05:04,231
<v Man>One more thing, how much would the fares cost? 


21
00:05:04,231 --> 00:05:12,815
<v Woman>Well, the bus is $1.8 in cash and the train is $10 each way. But, do you have a Travel Link Card? 


22
00:05:12,805 --> 00:05:15,818
<v Man>No, but I may get one before tomorrow. 


23
00:05:15,808 --> 00:05:34,800
<v Woman>Alright, if you have the card, you can pay considerably less. The bus will cost you $ 1.5 and the train to Harbour... sorry, wait, it will still cost you $ 10 because it is during rush hours in the morning, I'm afraid. Yet, if you could return at an off-peak time... 


24
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:36,441
<v Man>What do you mean by that? 


25
00:05:36,441 --> 00:05:46,813
<v Woman>All right, if you could begin your returning journey before 5 in the afternoon or later than 7:45 (a quarter to eight) in the evening... 


26
00:05:46,813 --> 00:05:52,037
<v Man>In fact, my plan is that I won't start to go back home until 8 o'clock anyway. 


27
00:05:52,037 --> 00:05:58,499
<v Woman>Then you can save a lot of cash using your Travel Link Card. You did mention that you were planning to buy one, didn't you? 


28
00:05:58,499 --> 00:06:01,683
<v Man>Yes, today, maybe later, I'll pick one up. 


29
00:06:01,673 --> 00:06:10,371
<v Woman>It means, with cash, it would cost you $10, but if with your card, you will only pay $7.15 for returning. 


30
00:06:10,371 --> 00:06:11,429
<v Man>Thank you. 

31
00:06:11,429 --> 00:06:13,587
<v Woman>Is there anything else I can help you with? 

32
00:06:13,587 --> 00:06:19,885
<v Man>Ah, yes. In fact, I would like to know if the Travel Link Card supports ferry services? 


33
00:06:19,885 --> 00:06:27,145
<v Woman>If the ferry services you say is Harbour City ferries that connect the northern and southern banks, then yes. 

34
00:06:27,145 --> 00:06:38,896
<v Woman>They are commuter ferries, one-way trip costs $4.5, but with the Travel Link Card you will enjoy a 20% discount, and the cost will be $3.55. 


35
00:06:38,896 --> 00:06:43,597
<v Man>So, $3.55 for it... What about the tour boats? 

36
00:06:43,597 --> 00:06:55,172
<v Woman>You mean those ferries going upriver on sightseeing tours for tourists? No, they do not belong to Travel Link company, and they only take cash and credit card. 


37
00:06:55,172 --> 00:07:01,180
<v Man>Oh, I see. So, I may believe that you might not know how much they cost for one tour? 


38
00:07:01,180 --> 00:07:16,213
<v Woman>Actually, I do know. I took a friend to the trip up river just last week. We determined to go an afternoon tour and it cost us $35 each. There is also a whole-day option costing $65. 


39
00:07:16,213 --> 00:07:18,600
<v Man>Thank you. You really helped me a lot. 


40
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:21,124
<v Woman>With pleasure. Do enjoy your trip!